  (label "VA_RAW" (at 74.93 104.14 0) (fields_autoplaced)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 79e44008-ac41-5b3e-b424-376311070d07)
  )
  (text "POWER: everything runs from the Pico Plus 2's own USB-C port (VBUS, 5V, up to 500 mA from a computer).\n+5V     = VBUS from the Pico (pin 40). Feeds the LCD, backlight, window LEDs.\n+5V_YM  = +5V through a ferrite: YM2612 and the two 74HCT541 buffers.\n+4V5A   = quiet analog rail: ferrite + 10uH/22uF+47uF filter + LP5907 4.5V low-noise LDO. Op-amps and headphone amp.\n+3V3    = made by the regulator on the Pico board.\nGND is one solid plane on both layers. The audio parts are grouped on the left, away from USB and the LCD,\nso digital return currents don't flow under them. (A split ground put the YM2612 bus over the audio ground.)" (at 25.4 22.86 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 6ecca64b-0843-50c7-8dc0-84e205c820ea)
  )
  (text "Mounting holes: M3, positions set by the enclosure. H5-H8 hold the LCD module's standoffs." (at 25.4 160.02 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 2e0d43f9-5690-5b43-b0c8-15d4d71d7daf)
  )
)
